From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: remoteproc: qcom,glink-edge: add wakeup-source

Some messages from a remote processor need an answer while the system
is suspended, such as an incoming call or SMS from the modem. Allow
wakeup-source on a GLINK edge, so that the edges which carry them can
wake the system up.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
Built with W=1 and dtbs_check; not tested on the device yet.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml
index e78a89c..67c0455 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,glink-edge.yaml
@@ -52,6 +52,12 @@ properties:
       ID of the shared memory used by GLINK for communication with remote
       processor.
 
+  wakeup-source:
+    description:
+      Wake the system up when the remote processor sends a message on this
+      edge, so that messages which need an answer, such as an incoming call,
+      are handled while the system is suspended.
+
 required:
   - interrupts
   - label
